<title>USA: Teamsters head asks Herman to encourage UPS talks.</title>
<headline>Teamsters head asks Herman to encourage UPS talks.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Teamsters President Ron Carey called Labor Secretary Alexis Herman Tuesday, asking her to get United Parcel Service back to the bargaining table, his office announced.</p>
<p>The Teamsters struck UPS this week and there have been no negotiations since.</p>
<p>&quot;Ron Carey did speak to Alexis Herman and asked her to encourage the company to come back to the bargaining table,&quot; a spokeswoman for the union said. &quot;She listened to what he had to say and said she would look into it.&quot;</p>
<p>No one in Herman's office was immediately available for comment. Earlier this week both Herman and President Clinton encouraged the two sides to negotiate.</p>
</text>
